    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0195" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg175"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 21, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>General Sherman telegraphed yesterday that he had been in error in saying that
                    the enemy had retreated to the Chattahoochee river. You will correct my No.
                    1,000 by this last information.</p>
                <p>All was quiet on the 19th, 20th, and 22d, at Petersburg; but Lieutenant General
                    Grant is not idle there.</p>
                <p>I am, sir,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
